<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<section xml:id="ClassPrep" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Class Preparation Policies</title>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Purpose</title>

        <p>
            This component of assessment has several purposes:
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <term>Get exposed to new content.</term> Each day in class
                    will be spent working on problems, so that I’m there to help
                    you when you and your teammates get stuck.
                    So some of the content will be introduced via video or
                    reading before class.
                    This has a couple of advantages: (1) you can go at your own
                    pace (retry, rewind, rewatch, change the speed, pause,
                    whatever!) and (2) your second exposure in class will likely
                    make more sense after you’ve seen it once!
                </li>

                <li>
                    <term>Generation.</term> This is when you attempt to solve a
                    problem before being shown how to do it.
                    This has been shown to help with learning and remembering.
                    It is often the case that this doesn’t feel like learning,
                    but the truth is that learning sometimes hurts a little!
                </li>

                <li>
                    <term>Help me tailor the class to you.</term> If everyone
                    says they understand the content of the class preparation, I
                    will not bore you with going over it.
                    If you ask a question on the class preparation I will do my
                    best to answer it.
                    If everyone seems confused we can spend more time on it.
                    Please answer the questions honestly so we can make sure the
                    class works for you!
                </li>
            </ul>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Using Preview Activities in Runestone</title>

        <p>
            Begin by going to
            <url href="https://landing.runestone.academy">
      https://landing.runestone.academy
    </url>.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you do <alert>not</alert> have a Runestone account, follow these
            instructions.
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Click “Register and Get Started”
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Under "Student in a class," click the button for "Sign
                        up &amp; Join”
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        This will take you to a page that allows you to pick a
                        username, password, enter name, email, etc.
                        <ol>
                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    Please use your real first and last name;
                                    you can use any email and username you want.
                                </p>
                            </li>

                            <li>
                                <p>
                                    Use "(your university’s full name)" for the
                                    institution.
                                </p>
                            </li>
                        </ol>
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Save your username and password somewhere.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Do NOT select that you are an instructor and want to
                        create a course.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Click on "Create Account."
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        On the next page, enter your course name:
                        GVSU-MTH202-02-Fall-26.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        While there may be another option to select the course
                        from a list, don’t use that option.
                        Again, just enter the course name as above.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Scroll all the way down and click "Enroll"
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </p>

        <p>
            If you <alert>do</alert> already have a Runestone account, log in,
            use the person icon go to the user menu and select “Change Course.”
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Then scroll down if needed and choose “Enroll in Another
                        Course.”
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Enter the course name: GVSU-MTH-202-02-Fall-26.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Scroll all the way down and click "Enroll"
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Feedback and Grading</title>

        <p>
            You get feedback via the video, other students’ answers, and in
            class.
            These are graded for completeness, not correctness.
            Make sure you watch any videos, do any reading, and answer all the
            questions on the Runestone Preview Activity and you will earn
            credit.
            Your overall grade for this component will be the percentage you
            completed.
            That is, if you complete all of the class preparation assignments,
            you earn 100% for this part.
            The preview activities are due 30 minutes prior to class start on
            class days.
            I will review responses at that time.
            Since the benefit of these assignments come from doing them before
            class, class preparation assignments done after class are not
            accepted.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Academic Honesty</title>

        <p>
            You may collaborate and use any resources you would like for the
            class preparations.
            That being said, please do not enter anything you do not understand.
            Part of the purpose is for me to pace the class appropriately -
            entering answers you don’t understand will mean you don’t get the
            help you need!
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</section>